   "id": "approach",
   "title": "Two armies on the road to Calais",
   "time": "24 October",
   "narrative": "After taking Harfleur, Henry marched his sick and hungry army towards Calais. At the Somme crossings and on the road north the French host, under the Constable d'Albret, finally got ahead of him and blocked the way near Azincourt. The English settled for the night in and around Maisoncelle on rain-soaked ground, while the French camped in the villages to the north. Henry ordered silence in the English camp on pain of losing an ear.",
