   "id": "french-deploy",
   "title": "The French draw up their battle",
   "time": "Morning, 25 October",
   "narrative": "At daybreak the French formed in a crowded order. A dense vanguard of about 4,800 men-at-arms dismounted stood in front, with the main battle of about 3,000 a bowshot behind. Some 600 dismounted men stood on each wing. Picked cavalry, 800 to 1,200 strong, waited on both flanks of the vanguard like horns, and a leaderless rear body of mounted valets filled the surplus. Archers and crossbowmen, unwanted in the front, were crammed behind.",
