   "id": "english-deploy",
   "title": "The English line between the woods",
   "time": "Morning, 25 October",
   "narrative": "Henry placed his army across a front of about 690 metres, with the woods pressing in on either side. About 1,500 men-at-arms stood four deep in three battles, under Camoys on the left, the king in the centre and York on the right. Some 7,000 archers under Erpingham filled the flanks, and each drove a sharpened stake into the soft ground. The exact line is reconstructed; the sources give only the width and the order.",
